# V20 integration overlay (apply after the combined durable-replay candidate)
# Target: payload/server.py exact blob f02cef6a0ffc202c75fbe71c520c72ac19ff876d
#
# This is an integration contract patch, intentionally not product-applied under ZERO-MINUTE.
# The exact final hunk must be rebased after V12/V14/V15/V16/V17/V18 because those patches
# restructure handle_openai_responses()/stream_openai_responses().
#
# REQUIRED CHANGE
#
# Current exact source ends stream_openai_responses() with:
#
#   finally:
#       if not task.done():
#           task.cancel()
#       await asyncio.gather(task, return_exceptions=True)
#
# That cancellation is unsafe after provider execution may have advanced the remote Notion
# thread but before the durable replay transaction has committed.
#
# After the combined durable-replay refactor, split transport cancellation from transaction
# cancellation:
#
#   - run_request() owns provider -> canonical payload -> strict durable publication;
#   - once provider execution has started, closing/cancelling the SSE consumer MUST NOT cancel
#     run_request merely because the transport disappeared;
#   - let the bounded request task finish its durable commit (or fail closed) under the normal
#     provider/request timeout;
#   - do not emit IDs/result after the client is gone;
#   - do not populate TurnAffinity/reservation before durable publication;
#   - if persistence fails, preserve persistence_blocked/fail-closed semantics;
#   - keep a strong reference to any detached commit task until completion and consume/log its
#     exception so asyncio does not drop an unobserved task exception.
#
# REQUIRED REGRESSION
#
# 1. Start streaming request with a fake provider that records remote progress.
# 2. Pause after provider progress but before durable publication.
# 3. Close/cancel the async SSE consumer.
# 4. Release the durable publication barrier.
# 5. Assert the core transaction finishes and exact replay record exists.
# 6. Retry in-process and after store restart: provider call_count == 1 and exact canonical
#    response IDs/call_id are unchanged.
# 7. Repeat with forced durable write failure: no TurnAffinity, no reservation, no client
#    result; subsequent retry fails closed before provider.
# 8. Cancellation before provider start remains abortable and creates no durable record.
